From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yuwei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:43:47 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Keep shapings: of layouts alike, and of words

`LayoutContext` keeps what shaping a layout's text gave (`shape/cache.rs`,
`ShapeCache`), for the next layout of the same text at the same scale,
styled the same in what changes shaping, with its out-of-flow boxes and
edges at the same places.

The shaper also shapes a segment a word at a time and keeps what shaping a
word gave (`parley_engine`'s `shape/words.rs`), only where shaping a word on
its own gives what shaping the segment whole does: left to right, not Arabic
or Syriac, no features that are off unless asked for, and with fonts whose
rules take a space with the glyph beside it at most (`shape/space.rs`,
`space_reach`: what a font's GSUB and GPOS rules do across a space). Words
around a space a font takes so are shaped again as one. A word that starts
with a default ignorable is shaped with the space before it: where a font
positions no marks harfrust does, and takes the default ignorables after a
base with it. An inline object is between words and is not kept.

In a debug build every text that took a shaping is also shaped whole and
compared (`same_shaping`). `LayoutContext::clear_shapings` forgets what is
kept, for fonts added. fontique's `SourceCache` keeps a font it prunes
weakly, so that loading it again while a kept word holds it gives the same
blob.

The tests make their fonts, with a rule or two each (`write-fonts`, a
dev-dependency).
